Define the trait that would discharge Flag 6:

trait Flag6Certificate {
    /// Returns a tempered measure that is claimed to satisfy both conditions of Flag 6.
    fn measure(&self) -> &dyn TemperedMeasure;
    /// Proof or reference that pure-point support equals the full set of non-trivial zeros.
    fn pure_point_support_exact(&self) -> SupportProof;
    /// Proof or reference that the absolutely continuous part is identically zero.
    fn residual_vanishes_identically(&self) -> ResidualProof;
}

enum SupportProof { Analytic{ref: String}, FiniteHeight{height: f64}, Absent }
enum ResidualProof { Analytic{ref: String}, Numerical{tol: f64}, Absent }

A complete capture of Flag 6 is a value of a type implementing Flag6Certificate in which both proofs are Analytic. The generated crate must ship only with Absent or FiniteHeight/Numerical defaults and must document that supplying Analytic proofs is equivalent to solving the open problem.
